<title>USA: Hilton Hotels sells $375 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Hilton Hotels sells $375 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from Hilton Hotels was priced Thursday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>The offering was increased in size to $375 million from an originally slated $300 million.</p>
<p>Hilton Hotels develops, owns, manages and franchises hotel properties, hotel-casinos, resorts and ownwership properties throughout the world.</p>
<p>BORROWER HILTON HOTELS</p>
<p>AMT $375 MLN	 COUPON  7.95 PCT  MATURITY 4/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.592  FIRST PAY DATE 10/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA1  YIELD 8.01 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS  SPREAD +110 BP    CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
